\title{NOTES-M7 - K1 elaborator, code stepper, code store, MATCH, comparison plans (owner: M7)}
\taxon{Report}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{machine}
\tag{performance}
\tag{truffle}
\meta{origin}{rlvm-machine/NOTES-M7.md}
\meta{moved}{2026-11-24}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\strong{Read section 8 first} (wave 6, 2026-11-24 afternoon): what code objects are for, measured on the native image; the tier hook; case trees that inline matchers; which switches are ready. Sections 1 to 7 are the state of wave 4 (the morning) and are kept as the description of the stepper, the blocks and the tests; where section 8 supersedes a statement it says so.}

\p{Files: \code{\verb~|Elab~}, \code{\verb~|Code~}, \code{\verb~|CodeStore~}, \code{\verb~|Match~}, \code{\verb~|Cong~}, \code{\verb~|CodeShow~} (claimed: the listing printer), \code{\verb~|Tier~} (claimed: the hook of the compiled tier and the heat accounting); tests \code{\verb~|M7*.java~}. \strong{Nothing of this package runs in v0}: every entry point answers "walk the term" (0) while its staging switch is off (\code{\verb~|SW_FACTS~} for plans, \code{\verb~|SW_TELE~} for telescopes, \code{\verb~|SW_CODE~} for bodies / rules / closures, \code{\verb~|SW_CASETREES~} for RULES) and in strict mode (\code{\verb~|M7ElabTest.nothingRunsInV0~}); the callers in \code{\verb~|Eval~}, \code{\verb~|Reduce~}, \code{\verb~|Rules~} and \code{\verb~|Infer~} test the same switches before they call (section 4).}

\subtree{
\title{1. The stepper under convention H7, and the other deviations from ISA.md}

\p{ISA 8.2 shows the stepper as a family loop over an \code{\verb~|ACT~} frame in \code{\verb~|W~} (candidate (i)). Under the decided convention (stepper-convention.md H7) it is written as follows.}

\table{
\tr{\th{\verb~|#~}\th{ISA}\th{As built}\th{Reason}}
\tr{\td{D1}\td{registers are words of the \code{\verb~|ACT~} frame; arguments are addressed in \code{\verb~|argRun~} "without copying" (1.3, 2.4, 3.3)}\td{an activation is a window of the register stack \code{\verb~|m.RS~}: \code{\verb~|RS[rb-3] = capRun~}, \code{\verb~|RS[rb-2] = ls~}, \code{\verb~|RS[rb-1] = xp~} at entry, then the arguments, then the registers. The arguments are \strong{copied} into the window at entry (\code{\verb~|Code.enter~}); operand modes A and R both index the window, mode C a slot of \code{\verb~|capRun~}. \code{\verb~|argRun~} of the frame is always 0}\td{a frame has no address until it is written (H7); the callers hold arguments in three places (a spine run for DELTA, scratch for APPLY and IOTA, nothing yet for TELE, whose \code{\verb~|g_i~} are produced one by one). One copy of \code{\verb~|arity~} words buys one addressing mode and makes the block independent of the caller's scratch, so the caller may suspend freely}}
\tr{\td{D2}\td{chunk directories installed by compare-and-set (3.3)}\td{readers are lock-free (acquire loads, one release store per block id and per row slot); writers serialise on the store's monitor}\td{a publication is a copy of a few dozen words; the monitor gives the same reader-side guarantees and makes "one block per role" (\code{\verb~|publish~} is first-wins) and "one sub-block per binder" (\code{\verb~|addSub~} checks the node hint under the lock) true by construction, which is what makes two workers build word-identical blocks}}
\tr{\td{D3}\td{\code{\verb~|Code.run(m, blk, pc, rbase, d)~} is entry and continuation step}\td{kept. The dispatch loop is \code{\verb~|Code.resumeAt~} (a \code{\verb~|resume*~} name: a family's dense switch is exempt from the 325-bytecode step limit, H10 rule 2); every instruction body is a small method. The entry step (H4: tick, call event, window, depth test) is \code{\verb~|begin~} + \code{\verb~|go~}; a spilled entry is the frame \code{\verb~|ACT[.., dst = DST_ENTRY, ..]~} and is ticked again when the driver resumes it}\td{H4}}
\tr{\td{D4}\td{\code{\verb~|TARG i, flags, dom~} is one instruction with several sub-judgments}\td{phases of opcode \code{\verb~|TARG~} in the \code{\verb~|x~} byte, each calling at most one judgment: \code{\verb~|TARG.INFER i, Lbind, Lnext~} (Tt = INFER(t_i); ONLY mode: bind and skip); the domain code, preceded by \code{\verb~|MATCH Tt, T(dom), i, Lbind~} when the domain is an open constant application; \code{\verb~|TARG.CONV i, D~} (CONV with the ER rule of \code{\verb~|eagerReduce~}, else \code{\verb~|fail(E_APP_MISMATCH)~}); \code{\verb~|TARG.BIND i~} (g_i = read later ? ARGV(t_i) : HOLE). \code{\verb~|TARG.EXPECT T(result), n~} is the result-pattern shortcut of TRET (B5). The site (argument terms in X, env, ls, mode, expected) lives in 8 site registers after the arguments}\td{under H the state of an activation is its pc. The frozen opcode set is unchanged}}
\tr{\td{D5}\td{\code{\verb~|CONG~} is elaborated rent-to-own (3.1)}\td{a plan is built at the first \code{\verb~|Cong.planOf~} once the fact record exists (the caller triggers \code{\verb~|Facts.sigd~})}\td{a few dozen instructions per position, no source term to walk}}
\tr{\td{D6}\td{leaves of a case tree are \code{\verb~|p ȳ~} (3.6)}\td{any term is a leaf, compiled in tail position}\td{the soundness argument of 3.6 does not depend on the leaf's form; \code{\verb~|casesOn~}-style heads are recognised by analysing the head definition (\code{\verb~|Elab.casesOnInfo~}), so matchers over any non-K, non-structure inductive type are trees}}
\tr{\td{D7}\td{\code{\verb~|RULE(r, j)~}: one block per rule}\td{one block per recursor with one entry per rule (entry word 0 = that rule is walked); arity = the largest rule arity}\td{one publication per recursor; the block is a function of the store}}
\tr{\td{D8}\td{sub-block "entry per number of applied lambdas" (3.4)}\td{entry j - 1 = "j binders applied"; j below the number of leading lambdas returns the closure of the rest, which is walked. Chains longer than 16 keep the first 16 in the block. The Pi that remains after a partial application of a TELE gets no sub-block. A body of more than 64 nodes gets none (3.4)}\td{bounds the code per binder; a block per telescope suffix tripled the code of Init.Prelude's telescopes (12,884 blocks against 7,698)}}
\tr{\td{D9}\td{a block's level pool (3.3)}\td{absent: every level and level list is an operand L / LL holding the id found in the term's own node, a base id; \code{\verb~|pubcheck~} verifies it against \code{\verb~|LevelStore.baseSize / baseListCount~}}\td{the elaborator consults no fact and derives no level}}
\tr{\td{D10}\td{\code{\verb~|KVAL d, k~} with a pool index}\td{the operand is the closed term (mode K); \code{\verb~|x~} bit 0 = the node stood in an argument position: the value is then \code{\verb~|ARGV~} of it (a suspension for an active term), as the generic walk builds it; \code{\verb~|x~} bit 1 = the term mentions a level parameter (the inline-cache key is then \code{\verb~|ls~}, else 0)}\td{decision 6}}
\tr{\td{D11}\td{LEAF blocks run "without a frame" (B11)}\td{LEAF is a header flag; under H no activation writes a frame unless a sub-judgment is suspended}\td{H1}}
\tr{\td{D12}\td{operand reads}\td{\code{\verb~|Code.val~} reads as the generic walk reads a variable, \code{\verb~|PEEK(GET)~} (\code{\verb~|Eval.atom~}), and faults \code{\verb~|E_HOLE~} on an argument or captured slot that holds HOLE; a capture list copies the binding raw (\code{\verb~|Code.raw~}), as \code{\verb~|PRUNE~} does. A register may hold HOLE (\code{\verb~|BUNREAD~}) and pass it to an APPLY}\td{the frames and values of both tiers are then the same records (verified, section 5)}}
\tr{\td{D13}\td{TAILAPPLY / TAILCALL overwrite the own frame}\td{TAILAPPLY is a call followed by the pop of the window (continuation \code{\verb~|DST_RET~})}\td{its arguments are scratch of the activation (H3: a tail return may own no scratch)}}
\tr{\td{D14}\td{\code{\verb~|BUNREAD f, i, d, L~}}\td{\code{\verb~|BUNREAD d, f, i, n, L~}: n = the number of arguments the following APPLY passes}\td{APPLY binds \code{\verb~|j = min(leading lambdas, n)~} binders and tests the body after j of them (4.3.1); the same test needs n}}
\tr{\td{D15}\td{\code{\verb~|SWITCH s, L0..Lk-1, Lx~}}\td{\code{\verb~|SWITCH s, I, L0.., Lx~}: the inductive type is an operand; a value that is not a constructor of I applied to exactly its parameters and fields goes to Lx (also a big-number or string literal, and a numeral when the Nat guards are not VALID)}\td{an ill-typed or stuck major must take the DELTA path}}
\tr{\td{D17}\td{\code{\verb~|let -> MKSUSP(value, LET) always (2.8)~} (3.4)}\td{a let value is compiled in position ARG (an atom, an inert application built at once, a plain suspension of an active term); \code{\verb~|MKSUSP~} keeps its LET bit but the elaborator does not emit it}\td{M2 changed the generic EVAL of a let to exactly that on 2026-11-24T10:26Z (NOTES-M2 D9: the LET suspension is INFER's; flagging the lets of an evaluated term made values OPEN and switched off Nat folding in lazy delta where the official kernel folds). The tier test showed it at once: 23 of 24,861 cases differed (a LET suspension against the closure in a captured slot) until the elaborator followed}}
\tr{\td{D16}\td{probe \code{\verb~|ELAB_AT~} is \code{\verb~|Op.ELAB_AT~}}\td{\code{\verb~|CodeStore.elabAt~} (reduction roles, default 1 since wave 6) and \code{\verb~|CodeStore.teleAt~} (TELE, default 10); system property \code{\verb~|rlvm.machine.elabAt~} (1..15) sets both}\td{the sweep of ISA 3.1; section 8.4}}
\tr{\td{D18}\td{\code{\verb~|tree ::= I.casesOn .. | I.rec ..~}, leaves \code{\verb~|p ȳ~} (3.6)}\td{a tree node may also be \code{\verb~|D args~} for a definition \code{\verb~|D~} that has a case tree of its own: \code{\verb~|D~}'s tree is compiled in place with its parameters bound to the argument terms (\code{\verb~|Elab.inline~}, section 8.3); an eta-reduced minor is a leaf}\td{the hot shape of every definition by pattern matching; the same composition of official steps}}
\tr{\td{D19}\td{RULES is used by WHNF only (3.6)}\td{also by the unfolding step of lazy delta for shape CASESON (\code{\verb~|Code.rulesCasesOn~}, switch \code{\verb~|m7a~}): \code{\verb~|I.casesOn~} itself, where no state of the official loop lies between the DELTA and the iota of one step}\td{section 8.5}}
}

\p{Frames of this family: \code{\verb~|ACT [blk, pc, dst, 0, capRun, ls, rbase]~} (\code{\verb~|Op.ACT_*~}; \code{\verb~|dst~} < 256: the window index that receives the awaited result; otherwise \code{\verb~|DST_RET~}, \code{\verb~|DST_ENTRY~}, \code{\verb~|DST_NONE~}, \code{\verb~|DST_REQ_APP~}) and five continuations of judgments whose K1 half lives here: \code{\verb~|ACT[1](v, k)~}, \code{\verb~|ACT[2](xb)~} (RULES), \code{\verb~|ACT[3](v, ar)~}, \code{\verb~|ACT[4](v, xb)~} (DELTA through BODY), \code{\verb~|ACT[5](xb, n, total)~} (IOTA through RULE).}
}

\subtree{
\title{2. Blocks and instructions as built}

\pre{\verb~|
block   hdr0 = len:20 | nreg:8 | role:4     hdr1 = owner row (0 for a sub-block)
        hdr2 = arity:12 | flags:12 | nentry:8          flags: LEAF 1, SUB 4, shape << 4 (PICK, PROJARG, CTORBODY, CASESON, MATCHER)
        hdr3 = 0 (sub-block: its binder term; CONG: the facts index)
        entry table: BODY 1 entry; RULE one per rule; RULES 1; TELE arity + 1 (0 = first TARG, k = "return the
        remaining Pi after k arguments", arity = the result code); sub-block one per number of binders applied
instr   op:8 | d:8 | n:8 | x:8, then n operands mode:4 | payload:28 (Op.MODE_*)
        MKAPP d, h, a..        KCONST d, D, LL       KSORT d, L        KLIT d, T        KVAL d, K
        MKLAM / MKPI d, T, B, c0..ck      MKSUSP d, T, c0..ck (x: LET)      MKPROJ d, D, I, s
        MOV, PEEK, NSUCC d, s      FIELDS d0, s (x = n)      JMP L      BEQ / BNE a, b, L      BKIND s, I(set), L
        BUNREAD d, f, I(i), I(n), L      SWITCH s, D(I), L0.., Lx      MATCH s, T, I(n), L      RET s
        APPLY d, f, a..      TAILAPPLY f, a..      WHNF / FORCE d, s      TARG (four phases)      TRET s
CONG    hdr2 = npos | PROP_STATIC; word 4 = lamArity; per position: class | UNREAD | rank, dep low, dep high
~}

\p{The elaboration scheme is the comment of \code{\verb~|Elab~}: three positions (TAIL, EVAL, ARG) that mirror EVAL and ARGV of ISA 4.2 as M2 implements them, so that both tiers build the same records.}
}

\subtree{
\title{3. Listings of ISA 3.7 as reproduced (\code{\verb~|M7ListingTest~}, from \code{\verb~|init-prelude.ndjson~})}

\p{Differences from the text of 3.7:}

\ul{
\li{capture lists show every slot up to the highest bit of the node's mask: \code{\verb~|[A0, _, _, A3]~} for the minor premise of \code{\verb~|Nat.casesOn~} where the ISA printed \code{\verb~|[A3]~} (the lambda's second domain reads the motive);}
\li{every entry of a sub-block is printed (\code{\verb~|B1 (1 applied)~}, \code{\verb~|B1 (2 applied)~});}
\li{\code{\verb~|BODY(Nat.casesOn)~} is LEAF by the rule of 3.4 (four class-p instructions); the ISA omitted the flag;}
\li{\code{\verb~|RULES(Nat.casesOn)~} is the ISA's line with the inductive type as an operand of \code{\verb~|SWITCH~}; \code{\verb~|RULES(Nat.add.match_1)~} is the one-level tree of 3.6 (\code{\verb~|TAILAPPLY A3, A1~} / \code{\verb~|FIELDS; TAILAPPLY A4, A1, r1~});}
\li{\code{\verb~|RULE(Nat.rec, succ)~} is the ISA's line with the two registers numbered in emission order;}
\li{\code{\verb~|TELE(congrArg)~}: \code{\verb~|TARG~} is the group of D4; the active arguments \code{\verb~|f a₁~}, \code{\verb~|f a₂~} of the result are \code{\verb~|BKIND g4, neutral / MKSUSP / MKAPP~} groups, the K0-equivalent form (decision 8), where the ISA printed \code{\verb~|APPLY~} (the strict form of open question 1; \code{\verb~|Elab.State.strictArgs~} emits it; off, it changes value ids);}
\li{\code{\verb~|CONG(congrArg)~}: positions 2-4 are \code{\verb~|PROOFL~} (their sorts \code{\verb~|u~}, \code{\verb~|u~}, \code{\verb~|imax u v~} are manifest and can be zero: \code{\verb~|congrArg.{0,0}~} compares proofs there), which is what 6.1 and 3.5 specify; the listing printed \code{\verb~|SAME~}. \code{\verb~|CONG(HAdd.hAdd)~} is the listing's. Probe ranks follow the rule of 6.1 (for \code{\verb~|HAdd.hAdd~} position 5 is probed before 3; the remark under the listing says 3). Both plans are reproduced twice: from a hand-made record of the layout of 3.5 and from the record M5's \code{\verb~|SIGD~} derives;}
\li{class TYPE: "the domain is a sort or a Pi telescope that ends in one" (6.1), \strong{or} its sort is manifest and of the form \code{\verb~|l + 2~} (the domain lives two universes up: \code{\verb~|outParam (Type w)~} in \code{\verb~|HAdd.hAdd~}, which the listing classifies TYPE). Both are compare classes; only the probe order differs;}
\li{the \code{\verb~|slvl~} / \code{\verb~|rlvl~} part of the TELE header is M5's fact record and is not printed.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{4. How the other packages call K1 (all in the main tree since 2026-11-24T10:41Z)}

\table{
\tr{\th{Caller (owner)}\th{Call}\th{Switch}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Reduce.delta~} (M3): BODY on the spine, then APPLY of the arguments beyond the arity; \code{\verb~|Reduce.iotaRule~}: RULE on the rule's arguments}\td{\code{\verb~|Code.blockFor(row, ROLE_BODY / ROLE_RULE)~}, \code{\verb~|Code.arityOf~}, \code{\verb~|Code.hasEntry~}, \code{\verb~|Code.callRun~}, \code{\verb~|Code.callRule~}}\td{\code{\verb~|SW_CODE~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Rules.rules~} / \code{\verb~|Rules.unfold~} (M3)}\td{\code{\verb~|Code.rules(m, v, d)~}: the complete RULES judgment}\td{\code{\verb~|SW_CASETREES~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Eval.applyFrom~}, \code{\verb~|Eval.instBody~} (M2)}\td{\code{\verb~|Code.closureBlock~} (kept in the CODE memo), \code{\verb~|Code.arityOf~}, \code{\verb~|Code.hasEntry~}, \code{\verb~|Code.callClosure~}}\td{\code{\verb~|SW_CODE~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Infer.inferApp~} (\code{\verb~|teleApp~}), \code{\verb~|Infer.vtypeNode~} (\code{\verb~|teleNeu~}) (M5)}\td{\code{\verb~|Code.blockFor(row, ROLE_TELE)~}, \code{\verb~|Code.tele~}, \code{\verb~|Code.teleValues~}, \code{\verb~|Code.arityOf~}; the arguments beyond the block's arity continue in the generic TWALK / NEU loop}\td{\code{\verb~|SW_TELE~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Cargs~} (M4)}\td{\code{\verb~|Facts.sigd~} (derive), then \code{\verb~|Cong.planOf~} + \code{\verb~|Cong.words / base / positions / lamArity / classWord / dep / propStatic~}}\td{\code{\verb~|SW_FACTS~}; \strong{not wired, and not to be wired as specified} (section 8.6: skipped positions are not the official verdict)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Eval.codeArity~} (M2, since 14:54Z)}\td{\code{\verb~|Code.entryFor(m, blk, n)~}: the entry of a closure's block for n arguments}\td{\code{\verb~|SW_CODE~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Conv.unfoldT / unfoldS~} -> \code{\verb~|Rules.unfoldLazy~} (M4, M3, since 15:05Z / 15:3xZ)}\td{\code{\verb~|Code.rulesCasesOn(m, v, d)~}: the CASESON tree as the unfolding step of lazy delta}\td{\code{\verb~|SW_CASETREES~} + \code{\verb~|m7a~}}}
\tr{\td{a compiled tier (\code{\verb~|rlvm-truffle~}, T2)}\td{class \code{\verb~|Tier~} (section 8.2)}\td{\code{\verb~|t2~}}}
}

\p{So \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.machine.switches=code,tele,casetrees~} runs K1 in the main tree. One rule for every caller of a block, learnt the hard way while the TELE hook was being re-anchored on M5's new TWALK: \strong{capture \code{\verb~|m.ep~} (and any other stack mark) before the call}. A block that is suspended leaves the environments of its sub-judgments on \code{\verb~|es~} (H7), so a continuation frame written with the \code{\verb~|m.ep~} read after the call restores a wrong mark; the declaration then ends with a machine that is not idle and is declined (\code{\verb~|E_INTERNAL~}, 9 units of Init, all on terms deeper than the host bound; never a wrong verdict). M5's published hook does it right; \code{\verb~|M7BenchTest.init~} asserts that every configuration accepts the same units.}
}

