\p{Peak RSS with \code{\verb~|code,casetrees~} (one worker): reachability 311 MiB (v0: 1,151 to 1,348), Init 203 MiB, Std 348 MiB, Cedar slice 182 MiB. Every row: the machine accepted every unit it was given, 0 declined (4,224 / 8,064 / 57,938 / 100,096).}

\p{Reading: the reduction roles (BODY, RULE, case trees, closure sub-blocks) are what code objects are for. With the trees of 8.3 the machine checks reachability in 1.54 to 1.58 s of CPU (gruszka on this host: 3.97 s, nano-lean 2.08 s; the reference engine 12.2 s) and saves 16 \% on Init and 14 \% on Std; on the Cedar slice, where 82 \% of the work is inference and conversion of open terms, they save 5 \%. TELE as built gains nothing (8.5). Nothing of it changes a verdict (8.7).}
}

\subtree{
\title{8.2 The tier hook and heat (class \code{\verb~|Tier~}; ISA 8.3, 8.4)}

\p{Published 13:39Z in the shape the Truffle agent asked for (requests.log 13:30Z):}

\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|public abstract class Tier { public interface Factory { Tier create(Machine m); } public static Factory factory(); public abstract int run(Machine m, int blk, int pc, int rb, int d); }~}: one \code{\verb~|Tier~} per \code{\verb~|Machine~}, made by the factory found through \code{\verb~|ServiceLoader~} (\code{\verb~|META-INF/services/rlvm.machine.Tier$Factory~}), once, at the machine's first declaration, \strong{only if the machine runs with switch \code{\verb~|t2~}} and never in strict mode (\code{\verb~|Tier.beginDecl~}); \code{\verb~|Tier.set(m, tier)~} / \code{\verb~|Tier.of(m)~} for tests and wrappers.}
\li{The stepper offers every activation to the tier: in \code{\verb~|Code.go~} after the depth test (an activation that is too deep becomes the frame \code{\verb~|ACT[.., DST_ENTRY, ..]~} first and is offered when it is resumed) and in \code{\verb~|Code.run~} (every resume: the awaited result is already in the window word the frame named, so the window is the whole state). \code{\verb~|run~} returns the result or the signal with the effects of \code{\verb~|Code.resumeAt~}, or \code{\verb~|Op.MISS~} before it changed anything.}
\li{What a tier may call: \code{\verb~|Tier.interpret(m, code, blk, pc, rb, d)~} (the stepper; \code{\verb~|code~} = \code{\verb~|Tier.block(m, blk)~}, a copy of the block with base 0), \code{\verb~|Tier.step(..)~} (ONE instruction through the stepper's own body \code{\verb~|Code.resumeOne~}: the next pc, or \code{\verb~|Tier.DONE~} with \code{\verb~|Tier.result(m)~}), \code{\verb~|Tier.reg / setReg / operand / cap / ls / suspend / leave~}, \code{\verb~|Tier.blockCount / describe~}. For a bridge class in package \code{\verb~|rlvm.machine~} the helpers \code{\verb~|Code.val, raw, isNat, ctorIndex, icGet, susp~} are package-private and their signatures are frozen (a change is announced in requests.log first).}
\li{Heat is independent of a tier: \code{\verb~|Tier.Heat h = Tier.heat(engine)~} switches the accounting on for the engine's sessions: entries per block and session (\code{\verb~|int[]~}, no shared word written), one entry in 64 timed with \code{\verb~|System.nanoTime~} (inclusive, and "self" = without the blocks entered inside), \code{\verb~|h.entries / nanos / selfNanos / timed / spentNanos / report(top)~}, \code{\verb~|h.listen((heat, m, blk) -> .., 4096)~} on the worker thread (ISA 8.3).}
\li{Cost when nobody asked: one field load and test per activation (\code{\verb~|m.x7.hooked~}). Batch 2: Init, code,casetrees: 7.12 s on the integrator's image, 7.21 / 7.13 s with the hook; Std 12.38 against 12.25 / 12.47; no difference.}
\li{Tests: \code{\verb~|M7TierHookTest~} (fast): a tier that steps every activation with \code{\verb~|Tier.step~}, one that takes every second activation and answers MISS on the others, and one that calls \code{\verb~|Tier.interpret~}, give the K0 value ids of \code{\verb~|M7Tier~} under D = 128 and D = 0; every activation is counted once; without \code{\verb~|t2~} and without \code{\verb~|Tier.heat~} a session is not hooked.}
\li{\code{\verb~|M7HeatTest~} (a tool, slow group): the heat report of an export (\code{\verb~|work/status/machine-M7-heat-<export>-<switches>.txt~}). Init, code,casetrees, threshold 10 (before 8.3): 6,425 blocks / 869 KiB; \strong{293 blocks (34 KiB) take 92.8 \% of the 10.4 M entries}, 885 blocks 98.3 \%; 3,795 of the blocks are closure sub-blocks (440 KiB), 822 of them never entered. Reachability: 1,770 blocks / 213 KiB; 43 blocks take 95.9 \% of 4.43 M entries. The hot set is what R13 says: a few hundred blocks of the core library (\code{\verb~|List.rec~}, \code{\verb~|List.casesOn~}, \code{\verb~|*.match_1~}, the \code{\verb~|._f~} functionals, \code{\verb~|Int.add~}, \code{\verb~|Decidable.casesOn~}).}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{8.3 Case trees that inline the matchers they call (kept; part of \code{\verb~|casetrees~})}

\p{The heat report showed the pattern behind most activations: a definition by pattern matching is \code{\verb~|f := fun .. => f.match_1 motive x (fun fields => rhs1) (fun fields => rhs2) ..~} (also the \code{\verb~|._f~} functionals of structural recursion, which are over-applied: \code{\verb~|.. f~}). K1 as delivered ran three activations per unfolding (\code{\verb~|BODY(f)~}, \code{\verb~|RULES(f.match_1)~}, the alternative's sub-block) and built the motive closure, every alternative's closure and the matcher application to throw all but one away.}

\p{\code{\verb~|Elab.inline~} (with \code{\verb~|leaf~}, \code{\verb~|leafApply~}, \code{\verb~|betaLeaf~}, \code{\verb~|resolve~}): a tree node \code{\verb~|D a_1 .. a_n~} whose head is a definition with a case tree of its own (\code{\verb~|fun p_1 .. p_q => tree~}, \code{\verb~|n >= q~}) is compiled in place. \code{\verb~|D~}'s parameters are bound to the argument TERMS (\code{\verb~|DEFER~} environment entries: term + the environment region it is a term of + its owner), which are compiled only where the tree uses them: a major premise that is a parameter is \code{\verb~|ARGV~} of its argument (compiled once at the node, where it dominates every arm); a leaf \code{\verb~|p ȳ~} whose \code{\verb~|p~} is bound to a lambda of the caller is a static beta (ISA 3.4 "app, lambda head"): the right-hand side is compiled in tail position, in a copy of the caller's environment, with its binders bound to the FIELDS registers (HOLE for unread ones, B6), as a nested tree if it is one; arguments beyond \code{\verb~|q~} are applied to the leaves. An eta-reduced minor (\code{\verb~|Nat.casesOn x a b~}) is a leaf \code{\verb~|b fields~}. From \code{\verb~|D~}'s own value only tree nodes and leaves \code{\verb~|p ȳ~} (ȳ: fields, parameters, constants without level parameters) are compiled, never a term that depends on \code{\verb~|D~}'s level parameters: the block runs under the substitution of the role. A definition that is not of that form is not inlined and the caller's application is compiled as before (a failed attempt leaves nothing: \code{\verb~|inline~} resets \code{\verb~|bad~}, the caller restores the emission state).}

\p{Soundness: ISA 3.6 unchanged - the result is the composition of DELTA(f), DELTA(D), the recursor rules and beta on the same arguments; K-like and structure-like recursors are excluded as before; a stuck major leaves the block with NONE and the caller takes the DELTA path. It is used where RULES is used: by WHNF (\code{\verb~|Rules.unfold~}), not by the two-sided lazy-delta step.}

\table{
\tr{\th{code,casetrees, one worker}\th{ticks}\th{records made}\th{run words}\th{activations}\th{APPLY}\th{RULES blocks}}
\tr{\td{reachability, trees of ISA 3.6}\td{16.48 M}\td{9.08 M}\td{50.2 M}\td{4.43 M}\td{2.36 M}\td{71}}
\tr{\td{reachability, with inlining}\td{10.14 M}\td{5.59 M}\td{27.3 M}\td{2.28 M}\td{0.71 M}\td{112}}
\tr{\td{Init, trees of ISA 3.6}\td{66.5 M}\td{36.1 M}\td{159.1 M}\td{10.4 M}\td{4.63 M}\td{148}}
\tr{\td{Init, with inlining}\td{63.9 M}\td{35.3 M}\td{153.7 M}\td{9.5 M}\td{4.01 M}\td{231}}
\tr{\td{Cedar slice, trees of ISA 3.6}\td{17.53 M}\td{9.30 M}\td{-}\td{1.15 M}\td{-}\td{84}}
\tr{\td{Cedar slice, with inlining}\td{17.35 M}\td{9.23 M}\td{96.2 M}\td{1.10 M}\td{1.65 M}\td{115}}
}

\p{CPU and instructions: 8.1 (rows "without inlining" use \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.machine.m7.inline=off~}, the A/B toggle of \code{\verb~|CodeStore.inlineTrees~}; it also switches the eta-reduced minors off).}

\p{Tier equivalence (\code{\verb~|M7TierTest~}, default group): the case-tree test now runs every tree on every combination of constructors (and a stuck variable) for up to four major premises that are parameters, 120 combinations at most per constant: init-prelude 10,324 RULES cases (722 before), 966 trees fired, \strong{10,090 identical value ids, 0 different, 0 equal only up to PEEK}, 234 ill-typed applications failing in both tiers, D = 128 and D = 0. (The tree now runs before the K0 normalisation of the same case: the K0 WHNF of \code{\verb~|Nat.succ (suspension)~} forces the suspension to look for a literal, and a tree that ran after it was handed the value by MKSUSP where K0 itself had built the suspension - two cases "equal up to PEEK" that were an artefact of the order, ISA 2.1.)}
}

\subtree{
\title{8.4 Other changes to the stepper and the store (kept)}

\table{
\tr{\th{Change}\th{Evidence}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Code.addressOf~}: block id -> address kept per session (one plain load instead of two acquire loads per lookup; \code{\verb~|hasEntry~} did four)}\td{Init code,casetrees 118.8 -> 118.5 G instructions; batch 2 CPU flat (7.21 / 7.13 -> 7.10 / 7.19 s)}}
\tr{\td{operands of MKAPP / APPLY / TAILAPPLY read in the loop (registers and arguments without a call per operand); KCONST of a level-polymorphic constant answered by the site's inline cache (the IC table of KVAL) instead of the LSUB cache + the CHEAD cache; \code{\verb~|Code.entryFor(m, blk, n)~} for closures (M2 adopted it 14:54Z: no walk of the lambda chain per APPLY through a block)}\td{together, against the image of one pull earlier (M6's pooling is in the difference): Init 118.5 -> 117.3 G, reachability 29.2 -> 28.5 G, Cedar slice 46.2 -> 45.9 G; tier test identical}}
\tr{\td{rent-to-own thresholds per role: reduction roles at the FIRST request (\code{\verb~|CodeStore.REDUCE_AT = 1~}), TELE at the tenth; \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.machine.elabAt=N~} sets both}\td{instructions per run at threshold 10 / 1 (image of 15:11Z): reachability 17.8 / 17.8 G, Cedar slice 37.9 / 37.8, Init 108.2 / 108.1, Std 177.8 / 177.7; CPU s in batch 3: reachability 1.54, 1.58 / 1.68, 1.57; Cedar slice 2.55, 2.46 / 2.43, 2.48; Init 6.25, 6.27 / 6.25, 6.47; Std 10.90, 10.65 / 10.72, 10.60 (inside the noise of that host; section 8.8); code on Init 0.92 -> 2.2 MiB; M3: perf/unfold-before-literal 7.9 -> 4.1 s; gate at threshold 1 clean (8.7)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Code.rules~} / \code{\verb~|rulesCasesOn~}: a head with the wrong number of levels answers NONE (DELTA says "does not unfold") instead of running a block under ls = -1}\td{fail-open; no input reaches it after INFER}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|Code.targConv~}: \code{\verb~|m.enterER()~} (M6-F26)}\td{request of M6, 14:46Z}}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{8.5 Experiments}

\table{
\tr{\th{Experiment}\th{Result}\th{Verdict}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|tele~} on the native image (batch 0, quiet host, single runs; batch 2 and 3, two runs)}\td{on top of \code{\verb~|code,casetrees~}, CPU s without -> with: batch 0: reachability 2.64 -> 2.91, Cedar slice 2.96 -> 3.13, Init 6.69 -> 6.72, Std 11.26 -> 11.27 (on top of step 1 + probes + code,casetrees: 2.52 -> 2.70, 2.68 -> 2.82, 6.36 -> 6.22, 10.76 -> 10.34); batch 2: 3.05, 3.02 -> 3.03, 3.06; 3.28, 3.28 -> 3.27, 3.43; 7.10, 7.19 -> 7.00, 7.18; 12.41, 12.41 -> 12.47, 12.64; batch 3 (with 8.3): 1.54, 1.58 -> 1.69, 1.56; 2.55, 2.46 -> 2.53, 2.50; 6.25, 6.27 -> 6.53, 6.31; 10.90, 10.65 -> 11.07, 10.78}\td{rejected as a default: no corpus gains, the Cedar slice loses. With TELE the machine makes 10 \% fewer records on Init (36.1 -> 32.5 M; EVAL calls 4.7 -> 2.4 M) but enters 5.4 M more activations, each a window + 4 to 6 dispatched instructions per argument where M5's telescope-mode TWALK is straight Java; in v0 sessions its KVAL inline caches are cold in every declaration (400 k misses on Init). The role stays behind \code{\verb~|tele~}, elaborated at the tenth request. Not tried: TELE for VTYPE only (\code{\verb~|teleValues~}, no INFER / CONV per argument)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|m7a~}: the CASESON tree as the unfolding step of lazy delta (\code{\verb~|Code.rulesCasesOn~}; state-exact: for \code{\verb~|I.casesOn~} itself no state of the official loop lies between the DELTA and the iota of one \code{\verb~|lazy_delta_reduction_step~})}\td{with fakes of \code{\verb~|Rules.unfoldLazy~} / \code{\verb~|Conv.unfoldT,S~} (batch 2): Init 7.10, 7.19 -> 6.77, 6.88 s (-4.5 \%; 118.5 -> 115.4 G), Std 12.41, 12.41 -> 12.20, 12.29 (-1.3 \%; 194.3 -> 190.6 G), Cedar slice 3.28, 3.28 -> 3.24, 3.29, reachability 3.05, 3.02 -> 3.02, 3.06; gate clean on tutorial + bugs + four corpora}\td{kept; behind \code{\verb~|casetrees,m7a~}; active since M3's \code{\verb~|Rules.unfoldLazy~} (15:05Z) and M4's \code{\verb~|Conv.unfoldT / unfoldS~} (15:24Z). On the main tree of 15:39Z (real call sites), instructions per run \code{\verb~|code,casetrees~} -> \code{\verb~|+m7a~}: Init 109.8 -> 107.1 G, Std 187.3 -> 184.0 G, Cedar slice 40.0 -> 39.8 G, reachability 17.9 -> 17.8 G; ticks on Init 63.5 M -> 59.7 M; gate 8.7}}
\tr{\td{elaboration threshold 1 / 3 / 10 for the reduction roles}\td{instructions equal on Init, the Cedar slice and reachability (118.4 / 118.4 / 118.5 G; 46.2; 29.2); code on Init 2.2 / - / 0.9 MiB; M3: perf/unfold-before-literal 7.9 -> 4.1 s at 1}\td{1 (8.4)}}
\tr{\td{negative cache / marker for roles that stay generic; a denser opcode numbering; an operand mode "register known not to be a suspension"}\td{not built: each is below 0.5 \% of Init by the profile (\code{\verb~|CodeStore.blockOf~} 0.9 \%, \code{\verb~|Code.resumeAt~} 1.0 \%, \code{\verb~|Code.val~} 1.7 \% of all cycles before 8.4)}\td{-}}
}

\p{Profile of the stepper before 8.3 / 8.4 (perf, Init, code,casetrees, \code{\verb~|work/m7/perf/init-k*.txt~}): class \code{\verb~|Code~} 10.9 \% of all cycles (\code{\verb~|kConst~} 1.8 \%, \code{\verb~|val~} 1.7 \%, \code{\verb~|resumeAt~} 1.0 \%, \code{\verb~|mkClosure~} 1.0 \%, \code{\verb~|arityOf~} 0.9 \%), \code{\verb~|Eval~} 15.1 \%, \code{\verb~|Values~} 14.2 \%, \code{\verb~|Runs~} 12.4 \%, \code{\verb~|Infer~} 11.5 \%; reachability: \code{\verb~|Values~} 32.9 \% (\code{\verb~|neu~} 17.4 \%), \code{\verb~|Runs~} 16.6 \%, kernel 11.7 \%, \code{\verb~|Code~} 11.5 \%.}
}

\subtree{
\title{8.6 What was not done, and why}

\ul{
\li{\strong{CONG plans read by CARGS}: not wired, and it should not be as specified: the soundness review (S-F2, 13:48Z) showed that skipping a proof or unread position (classes PROOF / UNREAD) accepts pairs the official kernel rejects, and M4 took B3 / B4 out of every switch set (14:33Z). What remains of a plan is the probe order, and the probes that would use it are order-only now. \code{\verb~|Cong~} stays tested on fact records and unused.}
\li{\strong{FIELDS(S)} (IPROJ): not elaborated. It is an inference role, not a reduction role; IPROJ is not in the profile of any of the four corpora above 0.5 \%.}
\li{\strong{B9 inside TELE, TARG.EXPECT with a caller}: not done; TELE is off (8.5).}
\li{\strong{Sub-block rent-to-own}: sub-blocks are still made with their parent (440 KiB of 869 KiB on Init at threshold 10, a fifth never entered). With the reduction roles at threshold 1 the whole code of Init is 2.2 MiB per engine; no need was measured.}
\li{\strong{K2 (derived rules for structural recursion)}: M3 has it (\code{\verb~|k2~}). What 8.3 leaves on reachability is exactly that: \code{\verb~|RULE(List.rec)~} and the minor premise of \code{\verb~|List.brecOn.go~} (0.47 M entries each).}
\li{\code{\verb~|M7HookedTest.all230~} (slow group): the integrator saw the K1 lane end \code{\verb~|perf/loop-unfolded-once~} as CRASH where K0 declines it. Not reproduced: alone, in-process, with \code{\verb~|tele,code,casetrees~} at threshold 1 the machine declines it cleanly (\code{\verb~|M7LoopProbeTest~}: BUDGET_MEMORY, E_MEM, 34.5 M records); the crash needs the other 229 files' garbage in the 6 GB test JVM.}
}
}

