\p{Every cell: \strong{0 differences (SOUNDNESS 0, COMPLETENESS 0)} on the units compared. The units not compared in the last two rows are declines of the machine with \code{\verb~|UNSUPPORTED_INPUT ... eager reduction~} (M6's rule of 15:07Z, not this package: 1 / 5 / 11 / 8 / 164 / 203 units), which the driver hands to the reference engine, and loop-unfolded-once. "all 230" = 226 files with \code{\verb~|-Xmx4g~} and the four memory-hungry perf files (app-lam, gf3-matrix-product, magma-list-deep-n36, magma-list-pair-n21) with the launcher's heap, one at a time.}

\p{Module tests on the published state: fast group green at every publication (the publish script); default group \code{\verb~|M7*Test~} green (\code{\verb~|M7TierTest.initPrelude~}: 25,824 cases, 25,590 identical ids, 0 different, 0 up to PEEK, 234 ill-typed applications failing in both tiers, D = 128 and D = 0; \code{\verb~|M7ListingTest~}: the listings of ISA 3.7 unchanged; \code{\verb~|M7CorpusTest~}: pubcheck on every block, two workers word-identical); slow \code{\verb~|M7CorpusTest~} on Init (126,664 blocks when every role is elaborated, RULES 1,400 -> 2,564) and Std (218,654; RULES 2,209 -> 4,019).}

\p{Switches I consider ready to be on by default, with the evidence above: \strong{\code{\verb~|code~}, \code{\verb~|casetrees~}} (together; with the reduction threshold 1 and tree inlining, which are not switches) and \strong{\code{\verb~|m7a~}} on top of them (M6 may give it its final name; it is meaningless without \code{\verb~|casetrees~}). Not ready: \code{\verb~|tele~} (no gain; the Cedar slice loses), \code{\verb~|t2~} (the tier is another module). M4's \code{\verb~|lazyeval~} sends the one-sided lazy-delta steps through WHNF and so through the trees of 8.3; it is M4's switch and M4's measurement.}
}

